    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d725">

                <pb facs="0773" n="759" sameAs="frus:frus1944v07/pg759"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.20112 RP/12: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Chile</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Bowers</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Santiago</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-03-10T18:00:00-04:00">March 10, 1944—6
                            p.m.</date>
                        <lb/> [Received 10:16 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>475. While British Embassy has tentatively agreed to and its representatives are
                    proceeding with us with the classification of the Proclaimed and Statutory Lists
                    nationals on the basis reported in my despatch 8862, February 12,<anchor n="93"
                        xml:id="d725-f1"/> the impression persists that they doubt the advisability
                    of presenting the Chilean Government with a specific program for the
                    liquidation, vesting, forced transfer and cleaning up of specific firms and
                    individuals as outlined. Furthermore, conversations with Pack and Royden<anchor
                        n="94" xml:id="d725-f2"/> lead us to suspect that possibly London also is
                    somewhat reluctant to the initiation of any program which would reduce the size
                    of the lists.</p>
                <pb facs="0774" n="760" xml:id="pg760"/>
                <p>The British Embassy claims to have submitted the whole matter to London for
                    approval more than 2 weeks ago but that no reply has been received.</p>
                <p>As we feel that no further time should be lost in submitting the program to the
                    Chilean Government, we hope the Department may find it possible to emphasize to
                    the British authorities in Washington the desirability of London’s promptly
                    instructing the British Embassy to proceed with the program on the basis
                    outlined in the despatch under reference.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bowers</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d725-f1" n="93" xml:id="d725-f1-content">
